From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:25:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: reset the station when association follows a timed
 out SA Query

A non-AP MLD that lost its association without a Deauthentication
(power, crash, a local interface down) comes back with a new
authentication and association. With PMF the AP answers status 30, runs
an SA Query, and allows the next association once the query times out.
handle_auth() keeps the WPA state machine and the station entries of a
PMF station, so the partner link entries of the earlier association
survive, and ieee80211_ml_process_link() refuses those links with "MLD:
link: Station already exists" (status 1), or the kernel refuses the link
station (status 17). The station then comes back with the association
link only.

IEEE Std 802.11be-2024 11.3.5.3 l) has all states of the earlier
association deleted at that point. Delete them in handle_assoc() once
the SA Query has timed out, before check_assoc_ies() runs: free the WPA
state machine, which the station entries of all links share, the way
handle_auth() does for a station without PMF, and then run
ap_sta_re_add(), which removes the station entries of the other links.
check_assoc_ies() then creates a state machine for the link that
receives the association. Keep the authenticated state that
ap_sta_re_add() clears.

A state machine kept past ap_sta_re_add() does not work: its owner is
the authenticator of the earlier association link, and ap_free_sta() of
the station entries of the other links deinitialises it or marks their
links invalid in it. The new association then has no state machine, or
its 4-way handshake fails on the MLO Link KDE of such a link in M2.

Only Open System and SAE authentication are covered, as FT and FILS keep
keys of the authentication in the state machine, and only drivers with
full AP client state, as in handle_auth().

Upstream hostap still refuses the links as of 2026-09-22 (24c033de8775).

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -4576,15 +4576,8 @@ static void handle_auth(struct hostapd_d
 				  hapd->own_addr, ETH_ALEN);
 		}
 
-		if ((!(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_MFP) ||
-		     !ap_sta_is_authorized(sta)) && sta->wpa_sm) {
-			struct wpa_state_machine *sm = sta->wpa_sm;
-
-			clear_wpa_sm_for_each_partner_link(hapd, sta);
-			clear_wpa_sm_for_all_sta(hapd, sm);
-			wpa_auth_sta_deinit(sm);
-			sta->wpa_sm = NULL;
-		}
+		if (!(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_MFP) || !ap_sta_is_authorized(sta))
+			ap_sta_free_wpa_sm(hapd, sta);
 	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
@@ -7429,6 +7422,25 @@ static void handle_assoc(struct hostapd_
 		goto fail;
 	}
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	/*
+	 * IEEE Std 802.11be-2024, 11.3.5.3 l): delete the states of the earlier
+	 * association. FT and FILS keep keys in the state machine.
+	 */
+	if (hapd->conf->wpa && (sta->flags & WLAN_STA_MFP) &&
+	    sta->sa_query_timed_out && ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta) &&
+	    FULL_AP_CLIENT_STATE_SUPP(hapd->iface->drv_flags) &&
+	    (sta->auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_OPEN ||
+	     sta->auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_SAE)) {
+		ap_sta_free_wpa_sm(hapd, sta);
+		if (ap_sta_re_add(hapd, sta) < 0) {
+			resp = WLAN_STATUS_AP_UNABLE_TO_HANDLE_NEW_STA;
+			goto fail;
+		}
+		sta->flags |= WLAN_STA_AUTH;
+	}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+
 	/*
 	 * sta->capability is used in check_assoc_ies() for RRM enabled
 	 * capability element.
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -275,6 +275,20 @@ void clear_wpa_sm_for_all_sta(struct hos
 	}
 }
 
+
+void ap_sta_free_wpa_sm(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta)
+{
+	struct wpa_state_machine *sm = sta->wpa_sm;
+
+	if (!sm)
+		return;
+
+	clear_wpa_sm_for_each_partner_link(hapd, sta);
+	clear_wpa_sm_for_all_sta(hapd, sm);
+	wpa_auth_sta_deinit(sm);
+	sta->wpa_sm = NULL;
+}
+
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.h
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.h
@@ -483,6 +483,7 @@ void clear_wpa_sm_for_each_partner_link(
 					struct sta_info *psta);
 void clear_wpa_sm_for_all_sta(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 			      struct wpa_state_machine *wpa_sm);
+void ap_sta_free_wpa_sm(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta);
 
 static inline bool ap_sta_is_epp(const struct sta_info *sta)
 {
